ove. A clean hydrogen company planting its flag inside the humanoid robotic supply chain.</p><p>But look closer and you'll see it's a growing trend and perfect application for clean hydrogen. In fact, Morgan Stanley projects the humanoid robot market could reach \$5 trillion by 2050. So whether or not that number is precise, the direction is clear and the energy question for those machines is very much open. Hydrogen companies are betting that question has a hydrogen answer.</p><p>If you want to see our recent report on hydrogen and robotics, we'll put a link in the description below this video. All this points to why the cost of hydrogen production matters so much.</p><p>And that's the work we're doing at New Hydrogen. Our thermal loop technology is being designed to use inexpensive heat instead of expensive electricity with the goal of producing the world's cheapest clean hydrogen. The robot era is coming and we want to make sure the fuel is ready. If you'd like to learn more about Thermal Loop, visit newhydrogen.com and check out our short explainer video. New Hydrogen is publicly traded under the ticker new H. Thanks for your continued support. That's it for this week. Thanks for watching and I'll see you again next time.</p>"
