        'transcript' => "<p>Hydrogen is stealthy, strong, and everywhere you aren't looking. Hi, I'm Steve Hill, CEO of New Hydrogen, with this week's top hydrogen news. Did you know that nearly 80% of the \$200 billion worth of hydrogen produced today is consumed by just two industries? If you guessed oil refining and ammonia production, you got it right. But behind those two heavyweights, a hidden hydrogen economy is emerging.</p><p>From the depths of the ocean to the chip in your pocket, here are the top 10 most surprising ways hydrogen is powering our world right now. Number 10, the grid's giant battery. When wind and solar produce more energy than we can use, we don't want to just dump it. We can turn that excess power into hydrogen and blend it right into our existing natural gas pipelines to store it for later.</p><p>Number nine, your kitchen pantry. Like it or not, hydrogen has been in your house for decades. It's used to harden vegetable oils into solid fats, which is how we get shelf stable products like margarine. Number eight, a boost for athletes. The wellness world is catching on. Hydrogen-rich water is being used by elite athletes as a selective antioxidant to neutralize the specific free radicals that cause muscle fatigue and slow down recovery.</p><p>Gimmick or not, minds are open for a role for hydrogen and fitness. Number seven, self-sufficient seas. On the high seas, vessels like the Energy Observer act as floating labs. They pull hydrogen directly from seawater using solar and wind, sailing the globe without ever stopping for a drop of fuel. Number six, the perfect glass flame. To melt glass, you need intense high temperature heat that electricity often can't match.</p><p>Hydrogen provides a flame that is not only hot enough, but also incredibly clean, leaving the glass crystal clear and residue-f free. Number five, bulletproof data centers. When the grid goes down, your cloud data has to stay up. Tech giants are now replacing dirty diesel generators with hydrogen fuel cells for clean, non-stop emergency power for data centers and hospitals. Number four, green steel. We're</p><p>Finally killing coal in heavy industry. Direct reduced iron technology uses hydrogen instead of coke to strip oxygen from iron ore, making green steel a reality with zero carbon emissions. Number three, making your microchips. Your smartphone wouldn't exist without it.</p><p>High purity hydrogen is used to etch semiconductors at the atomic level and clean the advanced lasers that print the most powerful chips on Earth. Number two, warehouse workh horses. Over 35,000 hydrogen forklifts are buzzing through the United States warehouses right now. They refuel in three minutes and run all day. A massive advantage for 247 giants like Amazon. And</p><p>Finally, number one, silent stealth subs. At number one, the German type 2 and two submarine. It uses fuel cells to glide through the ocean in near total silence. With no engine noise and no heat signature, it's effectively an underwater ghost. Hydrogen is already the invisible backbone of our most advanced technologies, but manufacturers are facing a tough decision. Get it cheap, but then it's made from non-renewable and dirty burning methane gas, or get it clean, but expensive via outdated electrolyer technology powered by solar or wind.</p><p>The world shouldn't have to compromise. And that's why New Hydrogen is working day and night to complete development of Our thermal loop technology. It's a system that uses just heat and water to produce the world's cheapest clean hydrogen. We're a publicly traded company under the ticker new H and we appreciate your support. To get an update on our development progress or to learn how Thermaloop works, Visit us at newhydrogen.com. That's it for this week. Thanks for watching and we'll see you again soon.</p>"
